# No browser checks unless asked

Do not use the browser, browser tools, screenshots, or live page verification unless the user explicitly asks in the current message.

This project rule overrides default “verify UI in the browser before finishing” workflows from user rules, communication rules, and skills (including design/redesign skills).

## Explicit ask (do it)

The user must clearly request browser work, for example:

- “ábrelo en el navegador” / “open it in the browser”
- “verifica en el browser” / “check this in the browser”
- “haz una captura” / “take a screenshot”
- “prueba el flujo en la web”

## Not an explicit ask (do not do it)

Do **not** open the browser for:

- UI, layout, styling, routing, or copy changes
- “implementa”, “arregla”, “rediseña”, or finishing a task
- Implied quality checks after visual work

```text
❌ BAD: change a component, then navigate/screenshot to “verify”
✅ GOOD: change the component, confirm in code, stop unless asked to open the browser
```

## If not asked

- Do not call `cursor-ide-browser` tools (`browser_navigate`, `browser_snapshot`, `browser_take_screenshot`, etc.).
- Do not start the app only to inspect it visually.
- Finish from code, tests, or existing terminal output. Do not apologize for skipping the browser.
